1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:08,302
Meet CoworkSuperUser: a public, data-free Power BI template that turns approved Viva Insights results into a clear adoption story.

2
00:00:08,303 --> 00:00:17,871
It connects observed reach, repeat use, habit movement, consumption, potential champions, and work-pattern context without turning usage into a performance score.

3
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:21,958
Start Here routes program owners to the right question.

4
00:00:21,959 --> 00:00:23,730
Is adoption building momentum?

5
00:00:23,731 --> 00:00:24,991
Who is returning?

6
00:00:24,992 --> 00:00:26,694
Where is usage sustained?

7
00:00:26,695 --> 00:00:28,313
How do work patterns differ?

8
00:00:28,314 --> 00:00:33,099
Begin with the decision, then open the page carrying the right evidence and boundary.

9
00:00:34,013 --> 00:00:37,715
Executive Adoption summarizes the selected population.

10
00:00:37,716 --> 00:00:39,998
Active users show observed reach.

11
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:43,153
Power and Habitual stages show sustained use.

12
00:00:43,154 --> 00:00:50,593
Latest weekly active rate shows the newest aligned week, while function comparisons show where enablement may need local attention.

13
00:00:51,493 --> 00:00:56,052
Weekly Adoption and Usage separates reach from recurrence and intensity.

14
00:00:56,053 --> 00:01:03,693
Switch views without clearing filters, then compare active rate, return rate, cohorts, sessions, and credits.

15
00:01:03,694 --> 00:01:10,169
Use exact values before relative color, and check rollout timing and coverage before calling a trend.

16
00:01:11,093 --> 00:01:17,783
Adoption by Attributes compares observed reach and sustained-use share across function, organization, or level.

17
00:01:17,784 --> 00:01:22,983
Check population and privacy first, then compare the group with the company benchmark.

18
00:01:22,984 --> 00:01:27,947
Treat the result as a program signal, never an employee-performance comparison.

19
00:01:28,861 --> 00:01:33,289
Habit Movement compares previous and latest available-history stages.

20
00:01:33,290 --> 00:01:38,072
Read improved, stable, declined, and sustained retention together.

21
00:01:38,073 --> 00:01:43,263
Interpret every change with its stage, then use department views to locate differences.

22
00:01:43,264 --> 00:01:47,608
New history or organizational change can also move classifications.

23
00:01:48,528 --> 00:01:53,337
Champion Identification finds an outreach starting point among sustained users.

24
00:01:53,338 --> 00:01:57,299
Global order uses active weeks, then average weekly sessions.

25
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,608
Department coverage reveals gaps.

26
00:01:59,609 --> 00:02:06,799
These are potential peer-enablement partners, not experts, top performers, or automatic candidates for personnel action.

27
00:02:07,728 --> 00:02:12,370
Sessions and Credits keeps frequency and resource consumption explicit.

28
00:02:12,371 --> 00:02:18,475
Read total sessions, total credits, sessions per active person, and credits per session.

29
00:02:18,476 --> 00:02:24,308
Switch between Overall and By department, and expand to pseudonymous IDs only when authorized.

30
00:02:24,309 --> 00:02:26,237
Neither measure proves value.

31
00:02:27,161 --> 00:02:32,851
Work Pattern Context compares supplied Viva Insights patterns across Cowork stages and time.

32
00:02:32,852 --> 00:02:36,515
Network and beyond-hours metrics appear only when supplied.

33
00:02:36,516 --> 00:02:40,456
The Non-user group is a descriptive reference, not a control group.

34
00:02:40,457 --> 00:02:43,932
Cowork use can coexist with a difference without causing it.

35
00:02:44,833 --> 00:02:53,535
Methods and Metric Guide defines each measure's source, calculation, grain, direction, caveat, and evidence class.

36
00:02:53,536 --> 00:02:56,283
Use it before quoting results or thresholds.

37
00:02:56,284 --> 00:03:03,283
A correct calculation can still be unsuitable when its denominator, privacy state, or evidence class is omitted.

38
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:08,830
Setup starts with two completed Viva Insights analyses in one partition.

39
00:03:08,831 --> 00:03:13,340
Build a weekly Person Query with organization and work-pattern fields.

40
00:03:13,341 --> 00:03:18,459
Build a Cowork consumption query with sessions, credits, and policy context.

41
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:22,864
Choose connector-only or faster export-assisted setup, then validate.

42
00:03:23,768 --> 00:03:33,768
That is CoworkSuperUser: one public report experience for reach, return, stages, consumption, potential champions, and work-pattern context.

43
00:03:33,769 --> 00:03:41,694
Choose the connection option that fits, build the two approved queries, review the guide, and turn evidence into an owned enablement action.
